        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Their definition is based on the following, generic observations, which are illustrated in Figure 147, Figure 148 and Figure 149. In Figure 147, the example is for a set of PriceRule elements and their associated EnergyFee definitions. In the first hour after midnight (00:00) a PowerSchedule limit of 15 kW is in place and only one PriceRule exists. In the next hour (01:00 to 02:00) the PowerSchedule limit has increased to 30 kW and there are three different PriceRule entries, which are stacked based on their PowerRangeStart value. The pictured EnergyFee values are just examples and not relevant for the definition of the PriceAlgorithm choices.",
